        "title": "Intro: The Financial Journey from Campus to Company",
        "content": "Listen friend! If you are sitting in your hostel room in a 10x10 square feet space, creating Figma designs on your laptop, training a PyTorch model, or scripting an app with friends to solve a college canteen problem — then congratulations! You are not just a student, but a **Student Founder**.\n\nIn the Indian college ecosystem, a massive socio-economic transformation has occurred in the last 5-6 years. Earlier, there was only one rigid target in the 7th semester — to grab a standard ₹4 Lakh to ₹8 Lakh per annum package from IT service companies (TCS, Infosys, Wipro) or core campus placements. But today, Gen-Z campus founders are building multi-crore startups from hostel dorms. Steve Jobs started from Apple Garage, Mark Zuckerberg built Facebook from his Harvard dorm room, and today student founders from India's IITs, NITs, BITS, DTU, IIITs, and Tier-2/Tier-3 colleges are leading India's new D2C, B2B SaaS, DeepTech, EdTech, and FinTech revolution.\n\nBut... understanding one brutal financial reality check is the most important thing for every college student founder:\n> **\"Making an awesome pitch deck, winning a pitch competition at a college fest, or building a working prototype is NOT the same as running a company. The #1 reason 90%+ startups fail in the global startup ecosystem is NOT a bad idea, but FINANCIAL MISMANAGEMENT, BAD UNIT ECONOMICS, AND RUNNING OUT OF CASH (RUNWAY EXHAUSTION)!\"**",
        "color": "#10B981",
        "emoji": "🚀",
