        "title": "Intro: The Financial Journey from Campus to Company (Part 2)",
        "content": "When you are a student, the cost of financial mistakes doubles because you don't have deep personal pockets, nor do you have any immovable collateral (property/house) to pledge for traditional bank loans. You need to understand the subtle nuances of business entities, registration costs, legal compliances, GST thresholds, Section 80-IAC tax exemptions, Cap Tables, Equity Dilution math, CAC/LTV calculations, burn rates, convertible instruments (iSAFE), and government grants — without retaining any ₹50,000/month Chartered Accountant (CA) or Corporate Lawyer in the initial days.\n\nIn this comprehensive, zero-fluff mega-guide, we will decode the complete financial journey of an Indian student founder end-to-end. From the first receipt of entity selection, zero-balance current account hacks, securing government grants (SISFS, BIRAC BIG, NIDHI-PRAYAS), calculating unit economics (CM1, CM2, CM3), designing Cap Tables, signing iSAFE notes, to negotiating Term Sheets — we will master everything in simplified **English**, with real-world Indian college examples (Rahul, Priya, Amit, Sneha, Kunal, Meera, Aman, Rohan) and step-by-step mathematical calculations.\n\nLet's start step by step!",
