        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Business Entities Comparison for Student Founders (Part 2)",
        "content": "### Student Founder Decision Tree: *When to Choose Which Entity?*\n\n```\n                              ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                              │            WHICH ENTITY SHOULD YOU CHOOSE?              │\n                              └────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘\n                                                           │\n                      ┌────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┐\n                      │                                                                         │\n       ┌──────────────▼──────────────┐                                           ┌──────────────▼──────────────┐\n       │   IDEATION & TESTING STAGE  │                                           │  FUNDRAISING & SCALE STAGE  │\n       │ (Revenue < ₹5 L, Zero VC)   │                                           │ (Raising Capital, Hiring,   │\n       └──────────────┬──────────────┘                                           │  Applying for Govt Grants)  │\n                      │                                                          └──────────────┬──────────────┘\n         ┌────────────┴────────────┐                                                            │\n         │                         │                                                            │\n   ┌─────▼─────┐             ┌─────▼─────┐                                                ┌─────▼─────┐\n   │    Sole   │             │  Udyam /  │                                                │  Private  │\n   │Proprietor │             │Partnership│                                                │  Limited  │\n   └───────────┘             └───────────┘                                                └───────────┘\n```\n\n> **Golden Rule for Student Founders:** \n> If you are just doing market research in your hostel room, building an MVP, or running a pilot trial at a college fest — START with Sole Proprietorship (free, zero compliance). Only incorporate a Pvt Ltd company when grant money or investor capital is ready to land.\n\n#### Quick Entity Selection Matrix (Table 20.1)\n\n| Parameter | Sole Proprietorship | LLP | Private Limited |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Cost to Set Up** | ₹0 (Free) | ₹5,000 - ₹15,000 | ₹15,000 - ₹35,000 |\n| **Compliance Burden** | Minimal (GST if >₹40L) | Low (Annual Filing) | High (Board Meetings, Audit) |\n| **Liability Protection** | None (Unlimited) | Yes (Limited) | Yes (Limited) |\n| **VC Fundraising Ready** | No | No | **YES (Only Option)** |\n| **ESOP Pool Creation** | No | No | **YES** |\n| **GST Registration** | Optional (<₹40L) | Mandatory | Mandatory |\n| **Best For** | Freelancing, Testing | Small Teams, Services | Fundraising, Scale |\n\n#### 4 Proven Zero-Balance Hacks for College Founders:\n\n1. **PSU Bank Basic Current Accounts (SBI / Punjab National Bank):**\n   - State Bank of India (SBI) offers basic business current accounts where MAB requirements are as low as **₹2,000** (Rural/Semi-urban) to **₹5,000** (Metro cities).\n2. **Neobanks & Digital First Corporate Banking (RazorpayX, Open, Jupiter Money):**\n   - Built specifically for modern tech startups in partnership with scheduled commercial banks (ICICI / Yes Bank). Offers zero-balance digital current accounts, automated vendor payouts, direct GST/TDS tax payments, and seamless API integration for your app!\n3. **DPIIT Startup India Bank Partnerships:**\n   - Leading banks (ICICI Bank Startup Ecosystem Account, HDFC SmartUp, Axis Startup Account) offer **1 to 2 Years Complete MAB Waiver** for DPIIT-recognized student startups!\n4. **College TBI Recommendation Letter:**\n   - If your startup is incubated at your college TBI (Technology Business Incubator), banks offer specialized Incubatee Corporate Accounts with waived balance rules.",
