        "title": "Business Entities Comparison for Student Founders (Part 3)",
        "content": "#### Documents Required Checklist for Opening Current Account:\n\n| Document Category | Sole Proprietorship Firm | LLP (Limited Liability Partnership) | Private Limited Company (Pvt Ltd) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Identity & Address Proof of Founders** | Aadhaar Card & PAN Card of Founder | Aadhaar & PAN of all Partners | Aadhaar & PAN of all Directors/Shareholders |\n| **Entity Proof Document 1** | Udyam MSME Registration Certificate | Certificate of Incorporation (COI) | Certificate of Incorporation (COI) issued by MCA |\n| **Entity Proof Document 2** | GST Registration / Shop & Establishment | Registered LLP Agreement | MOA (Memorandum) & AOA (Articles of Association) |\n| **Tax Registration Numbers** | Individual PAN + GSTIN (if applicable) | Entity PAN Card & TAN Card | Company PAN Card & TAN Card |\n| **Board Resolution / Authority** | Self-Declaration Letter | Partnership Resolution for Bank Account Opening | Board Resolution authorizing bank account opening |\n| **Address Proof of Business** | Utility Bill / Rent Agreement | Utility Bill / Rent Agreement of LLP registered office | Utility Bill / Rent Agreement of registered office |\n\n#### Startup India DPIIT Recognition — Step-by-Step Guide:\n\n1. Visit `startupindia.gov.in` -> Click **\"Register\"**.\n2. Fill entity details: Company name, CIN/LLPIN, incorporation date, address.\n3. Select industry type, phase of startup, and DPIIT recognition type.\n4. Upload COI (Certificate of Incorporation) and Board Resolution.\n5. Self-certify under 3 conditions: Entity not formed by splitting existing business, turnover < ₹100 Cr, working towards innovation.\n6. Receive **DPIIT Recognition Certificate** within 2-3 working days.\n\n**Benefits of DPIIT Recognition:**\n- 3-year tax holiday under Section 80-IAC (Turnover up to ₹100 Cr)\n- Self-certification under 9 labour and 3 environmental laws\n- Easy winding-up process (exit in 90 days)\n- Fast-track patent examination at 80% rebate\n- Access to Fund of Funds, SIDBI lending, and Govt grants",
