        "title": "Grants, Incubators & College Seed Funding",
        "content": "Student founders don't have massive personal capital at the seed stage. But India has a powerful, government-backed ecosystem that distributes **hundreds of crores of rupees in NON-DILUTIVE GRANTS** (free cash where you give **0% equity** and zero repayment debt) every year!\n\nIf you have a working prototype, innovative research, or solid business idea, you should NOT make the mistake of selling equity to a VC from day one. Let's analyze India's premier government startup grants step-by-step.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Startup India Seed Fund Scheme (SISFS)\n\nThe SISFS scheme launched by DPIIT (Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade) provides financial assistance to early-stage startups for proof of concept validation, prototype development, product trials, market entry, and commercialization via approved college incubators across India.\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │    STARTUP INDIA SEED FUND SCHEME (SISFS) FLOW   │\n                                  └────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┘\n                                                           │\n                                        ┌──────────────────┴──────────────────┐\n                                        │                                     │\n                         ┌──────────────▼──────────────┐       ┌──────────────▼──────────────┐\n                         │      UP TO ₹20 LAKH GRANT   │       │ UP TO ₹50 LAKH DEBENTURES   │\n                         │    (Equity-Free Non-Dilutive)│       │ (Convertible Debt / Equity) │\n                         └──────────────┬──────────────┘       └──────────────┬──────────────┘\n                                        │                                     │\n                         ├─ Validation of Proof-of-Concept      ├─ Market Entry & Commercialization\n                         ├─ Prototype Development               ├─ Product Scaling\n                         └─ Market Testing & Piloting           └─ Working Capital Needs\n```\n\n#### SISFS Key Details (Table 20.2):\n\n| Parameter | Details |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Grant Amount** | Up to **₹20 Lakh** (Proof of Concept) + Up to **₹50 Lakh** (Convertible Debentures) |\n| **Equity Requirement** | **0% Equity for Grants** (Non-Dilutive) |\n| **Eligibility** | DPIIT-recognized startup, not older than 2 years |\n| **Sector** | Sector-agnostic (All sectors eligible) |\n| **Application Channel** | Through recognized incubators only |\n| **Incubator Fee** | 10% of grant amount may be retained by incubator |\n| **Repayment** | Grants: No repayment. Debentures: Convert at next funding round |",
        "color": "#10B981",
        "emoji": "🚀",
        "interactiveType": "none"
