        "title": "Grants, Incubators & College Seed Funding (Part 3)",
        "content": "Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME) launches **MSME Idea Hackathon** every year exclusively for college students and young innovators.\n- **Grant Support:** Up to **₹15 Lakh per approved idea** provided to host incubators for developing the prototype.\n- **Additional Support:** Up to **₹1.00 Crore** grant for procuring specialized plant & machinery for commercial production!\n\n---\n\n### College TBI (Technology Business Incubator) & AIC Ecosystem\n\nIndia has 150+ NITI Aayog **Atal Incubation Centres (AICs)** and DST-supported **STEP (Science and Technology Entrepreneurs Park)** incubators operational in top engineering and management colleges (IITs, NITs, IIMs, BITS, DTU, IIITs, NIFT, Central Universities).\n\n#### What Does a College Incubator Provide to Student Founders?\n1. **Physical Infrastructure:** Plug-and-play office desks, high-speed fiber internet, meeting rooms, and conference halls at ₹0 or nominal rent.\n2. **Specialized Lab Access:** Hardware, AI supercomputing clusters, bio-labs, 3D printing equipment.\n3. **Legal & Accounting Support:** In-house CA/CS panels to handle incorporation, GST, and ROC filings at subsidized student rates.\n4. **Direct Grant Facilitation:** Incubators act as official nodal implementation bodies for SISFS, NIDHI-PRAYAS, BIRAC, and TIDE 2.0 grants.\n5. **Investor Demo Days:** Direct access to Top Angel Networks (Indian Angel Network, Mumbai Angels, Venture Catalysts) and VCs (Peak XV, Accel, Blume).\n\n---\n\n### Master Comparison Table of Top Indian Student Grants\n\n| Grant / Scheme Name | Nodal Ministry / Govt Authority | Maximum Funding Amount | Funding Nature (Equity / Grant) | Ideal Target Domain | Key Eligibility Criteria | Application Window |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Startup India Seed Fund (SISFS)** | DPIIT / Ministry of Commerce | Up to **₹20 Lakh** (Grant) + **₹50 Lakh** (Debt) | Non-dilutive Grant / Soft Debt | Sector Agnostic | DPIIT-recognized, < 2 yrs old | Year-round via Incubators |\n| **BIRAC BIG** | BIRAC / DBT | Up to **₹50 Lakh** | Pure Equity-Free Grant | Biotech / Life Sciences | Academic scholars / Biotech startups | Annual Cycles |\n| **DST NIDHI-PRAYAS** | DST / Govt of India | Up to **₹10 Lakh** | Pure Grant (0% Equity) | Hardware / IoT / Deep Tech | Innovative prototype stage | Year-round via TBI |\n| **NIDHI-EIR** | DST | **₹10K-30K/month** x 12 months | Monthly Stipend | All Sectors | Graduating students | Year-round |\n| **MeitY TIDE 2.0** | MeitY | Up to **₹20 Lakh** | Non-dilutive Grant | Health/Edu/Agri/FinTech | DPIIT-recognized | Annual Cycles |\n| **MSME Idea Hackathon** | Ministry of MSME | Up to **₹15 Lakh** + ₹1 Cr | Grant + Soft Debt | MSME-focused | College students / Innovators | Annual |\n| **PM FME** | Ministry of Food Processing | Up to **₹10 Lakh** (35% subsidy) | Capital Subsidy | Food Processing | Micro food entrepreneurs | Year-round |",
