        "title": "Case Studies & Student Founder Toolkit",
        "content": "Let's examine 4 deeply detailed real-world style Indian student founder case studies covering SaaS, D2C, Hardware IoT, and EdTech, followed by actionable financial toolkits and spreadsheet blueprints.\n\n---\n\n### Case Study 1: Aman & Rohan's B2B SaaS Startup (DevFlow)\n\n#### Background:\nAman (CS 3rd Year) and Rohan (ECE 3rd Year) at a Tier-1 tech college built **DevFlow** — an AI-powered developer workflow automation tool for engineering teams.\n\n#### Financial & Funding Journey:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        DEVFLOW FUNDING & EQUITY TIMELINE                               │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Month 0:  Incorporated Pvt Ltd (50:50 Split with 4-Yr Vesting & 1-Yr Cliff).          │\n│ Month 6:  Secured ₹10 Lakh DST NIDHI-PRAYAS Non-Dilutive Grant from College TBI.       │\n│ Month 12: Scaled to $2,000 (₹1.65 Lakh) MRR. Raised ₹40 Lakh iSAFE Note @ ₹5 Cr Cap.   │\n│ Month 20: Rohan left for US MS; 1-Year Cliff executed, 75% unvested shares returned.   │\n│ Month 24: Scaled to $15,000 (₹12.5 Lakh) MRR. Closed ₹3 Crore VC Seed Round @ ₹15 Cr. │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n#### Detailed Breakdown & Lessons Learned:\n1. **Grant First Approach:** By securing the **₹10 Lakh DST NIDHI-PRAYAS grant** in Month 6, Aman & Rohan paid for AWS cloud credits and student intern stipends without selling a single share of equity!\n2. **iSAFE Capital Efficiency:** In Month 12, when MRR hit $2,000, they raised **₹40 Lakh iSAFE** money in just 7 days without endless valuation debates.\n3. **Vesting Saved the Startup:** When Rohan decided to leave the startup after Month 20 to pursue MS in US, the 4-year vesting clause kicked in. Rohan retained only his vested 25% shares, and his unvested 75% equity returned cleanly to the company pool — preventing dead equity from crippling the company.",
        "color": "#10B981",
