        "title": "Conclusion: The Campus Founder Mindset",
        "content": "Being a student founder in modern India is an incredible privilege and a true economic superpower. You have low personal financial liabilities, subsidized hostel rent, high energy, access to top campus peers, and a supportive government grant ecosystem designed specifically to fund your vision.\n\nRemember the 4 core financial pillars of a successful campus startup:\n1. **Validate Before Incorporating:** Use Udyam/Proprietorship for early validation; incorporate Pvt Ltd only when grant money or investor capital is ready to land.\n2. **Leverage Non-Dilutive Capital First:** Exhaust SISFS, NIDHI-PRAYAS, BIRAC BIG, and MeitY grants before selling company equity.\n3. **Protect Your Cap Table:** Always enforce 4-year founder vesting with a 1-year cliff, and never give away more than 15-20% equity in early seed rounds.\n4. **Master Unit Economics:** Focus relentlessly on positive CM3 margins, healthy CAC:LTV ratios (>3x), and maintaining a minimum 6-month cash runway buffer.\n\nNow stand up, open your laptop in your hostel room, and start building the future of India!",
